experiment: samediff
  SHORT RUN — 300000 ticks against a minimum of 672000. derived: §63, M6 run one. Word A, a gap, word B, and a held-out readout
  asked whether B was the SAME word as A -- the smallest operation that
  cannot be done without holding something. A and B come from a BALANCED
  four-cell list, so 'same' is 50/50 and B's identity carries nothing about
  the label by construction. One round is 16800 ticks (four gaps: 200, 800,
  2000, 5000 ms), and 40 rounds is the floor for a held-out split at every
  gap. §61's decay gate is demoted to INTERPRETIVE here: the readout is a
  linear nearest-centroid and same/different is XOR, which a linear readout
  of a superposition cannot produce -- so a surviving trace of A does not
  make the milestone trivial. §61's larynx-silenced arm is renamed
  ACOUSTIC-silenced: quietecho took the voiced fraction 0.773 -> 0.000 with
  the articulator echo UNMOVED, so the knob cuts the self-heard loop only.
  §69 ADDS FOUR DOSE ARMS and they are the first that move something other
  than `voicing_threshold`: `stp_use` 0.20 and `stp_recover_ms` on a
  100/300/1000/3000 ms ladder, patched into the auditory->vocal projections
  of the SESSION'S BLOB COPY. `dna/default.toml` is never written and the
  shipped hash must not move. The dose is the MERGED tract because the
  kernel keys STP by the (source, target) module pair; §68 priced that
  substitution at 1.2744 against the excitatory limb's 1.3076. §69's
  primary MOVES to `vocal`: depression here does not feed `central`.
  §70 ADDS NO ARM AND NO TICK. It adds four FEATURE SPACES on the same
  trials, because §68 measured 153.5 SE in the delivered drive and §69
  measured 0.8 SE in the vocal spikes and nothing said what lies between:
  the MEASURED delivered drive `w*u*R/U` read from the live kernel at the
  moment of transmission (excitatory and signed), §68's own arithmetic
  `1-(1-U)^n` on the same trial's spike counts, and the vocal MEMBRANE.
  The primary is the PREMISE CHECK -- §68 simulated depletion host-side
  with no within-word recovery over pairs that never physically occurred,
  the kernel runs the real Tsodyks-Markram recursion, and nobody had
  compared them. Here A and B are one trial, so the comparison is PAIRED
  on identical spikes. §69's own columns must reproduce EXACTLY: nothing
  added here draws a random number or touches kernel state.
  Everything below is printed for debugging and is NOT a
  measurement; this run cannot pass whatever it reads.


