    -> §68's SEPARATION DOES NOT TRANSFER AT FULL SIZE. The level
       offset is §68's own disclosed optimism and is not the finding;
       what matters is that a readout of the SIMULATED drive beats a
       readout of the REAL one on the same trials, so §68's figure was
       inflated by the simulation and not only by its flag. The
       measured drive is the right basis, and the localisation below
       is read on it.
    -> THE CONJUNCTION IS NOT IN THE MEASURED DRIVE AS A READOUT CAN
       USE IT. The arithmetic transfers and §68's own statistic still
       separates, but a held-out readout of the delivered drive does
       not reach the bar — so §68's pair-d' priced an ORACLE over
       pairs and never a single-trial readout. Nothing downstream is
       at fault, and the gap is in §68's estimator, not the creature.

